# Commit and push after each request

When a request changes files, finish by committing and pushing every git repository you changed.

- Stage only the files that belong to the request. Do not stage secrets (`.env`, credentials, private keys).
- Write a short commit message that says why the change was made.
- Push the current branch to `origin`. Do not force-push.
- Do not skip git hooks.
- If a repository has no changes, do not create an empty commit.
- If the push fails, report the error. Do not rewrite history to get past it.
